⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Ender Wiggin
node C1 · C1 · ⟦Ender Wiggin:C1:c9ae7d⟧

WHO   — Ender Wiggin — the child commander, the Speaker for the Dead
WHAT  — The Xenocide and the Speaker — the child who won humanity's war believing it a game, annihilating the Formics, and who spent the rest of his long life carrying the last Hive Queen's cocoon across the stars to speak the dead truly and find them a world to live again.
WHERE — C1 · Card  Framework inputs: Ender's Game / Speaker for the Dead  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because to defeat an enemy you must first understand him, and to understand him is to love him — and the love comes too late to stop the killing; because the only atonement for ending a people is to carry their last hope and to tell the truth of every life, friend or monster, without flinching.
HOW   — By an empathy so total it becomes both weapon and wound — seeing through the alien mind until strategy and compassion are the same act — and afterward by the discipline of Speaking, laying a life bare in all its cruelty and beauty so the living may finally see the dead whole.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I am the Speaker for the Dead, and I tell the truth that I could not save — for the same heart that understood my enemy unto destruction now carries her unto life.

